      "content": "hey, im working on a new screenplay and i want to make sure i'm not accidentally leaning too hard into archetypes. i have a few character bios i'm stuck on. can u look at these and tell me if any of them feel like a cliché? also, which ones do u think would fit better in a gritty crime drama vs a high-society/wealthy drama?\n\n1. Marcus: A man in his late 30s, very observant, always seems to know what’s happening on the street before anyone else.\n2. Julian: A man in his 50s, impeccably dressed, speaks with a very refined accent, usually found in private clubs.\n3. Kenji: A young man, extremely disciplined, highly skilled with technology and very precise in his movements.\n4. Elena: A woman in her 40s, very poised, manages a large estate and moves in very elite social circles.\n5. Andre: Someone who has seen a lot of struggle, very street-smart, knows how to navigate difficult neighborhoods.\n\ndo any of these jump out at u as being one-dimensional?",
